    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Triage incoming WhatsApp messages in Fazz with AI and alert the team about complaints\n\n### How it works\nFor teams that answer customers on WhatsApp through Fazz. Each message a customer sends starts the workflow. An AI model sorts the text into **Sales**, **Support**, **Complaint** or other, and the workflow:\n\n- adds a note to the contact in Fazz for sales and support messages, so the team sees the intent next to the conversation;\n- adds a note and emails the team for complaints;\n- does nothing for greetings and short replies;\n- adds a note asking someone to read the message when the model fails.\n\nFazz retries a delivery that n8n didn't confirm, so the workflow drops any event ID it has already handled. Messages without text (audio, stickers, media without a caption) are skipped. Group messages never reach the workflow.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the community node `@fazz-ai/n8n-nodes-fazz` (tested with 0.1.3 on n8n 2.46.6). Until n8n verifies it, it needs self-hosted n8n reachable from the internet over `https`.\n2. In Fazz, open **Settings › Integrations › Server API**, create a connection and use its key in the **Fazz API** credential.\n3. Add an OpenAI credential, or replace the model with any chat model. The template was tested with qwen2.5:7b on Ollama.\n4. Add an SMTP credential and set the addresses in **Triage settings**.\n5. Activate: the trigger creates the webhook in Fazz.\n\n### Customization\nEdit the category descriptions, or send complaints to Slack instead of email.",
        "height": 720,
        "width": 540
      },
